1-Var:
: Var can be used in Constructor,Method and init block
:Var can not be used in Constructor/Method parameters or static/class vairables
:Lambda where the parameter type can be inferred
:A Var is always initialized on the same statement where it is declared
e.g var x=4
:the value of Var can change but the type can not
var x=20
x=50  //allowed
x="abc" //not allowed

:Var can not simply initialized to null; cast the null to a type first
var x=null  /not allowed
:var is not allowed in multi variable declarations
:Var is resered name but not a reserved word
  var var=9  //ok
:identifiiers can be called var but type names e.g. classes interfaces, enums

2- Private Method
:Introduce in java 9
:private methods can be both static and non-static
:as this is private method these are accessible within the interface
:As with classes you can not access a non-static interface method from a static method

Advantage
:reduce code duplication
:improve code encapsulation

